{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792337181,"nonce":"labEeRAfMcNd1H+BdYdXnAZ/fns=","message":"Two causes found with a wasm reproducer (a Haxe program that builds a canvas-like set of buffers, drops them and forces collections, run under `ash run`), fixed in 2963f365922ba2017c77e62d7e8486cd4d8cdb75 and 5c05c82c8d09e3c766485f2b1267ac625cab9f42. The issue stays open until ashui's chains come back from the demo.\n\nSlow mark. It was not the noscan bytes: 80 MB of Bytes marks in 2 ms at any object size. Resolving an address inside a multi-block allocation walked back one 128-byte line at a time through every block to the allocation's start, so any word that pointed into a large buffer, real or stray, cost 0.2 to 0.5 ms on wasm. A block that only continues an allocation is now stepped over whole. Reproducer: mark 45 to 50 ms per collection before, 2 to 5 ms after (85 MB live before, 54 MB after).\n\nRetention. The wasm32 heap lies at about 10 MB to 512 MB, which is the range of Haxe field hashes (29 bits). The class lookup, field-index, interface and mark tables are scanned like any object, so a hash in them looked like a heap pointer and kept whatever lay at that address, large buffers included. They are now allocated pointer-free. Live bytes after the build went from 85 MB to 54 MB.\n\nNot the roots: the stack scan is [sp, top), 1 KB in the reproducer, and the fiber window only applies to a suspended main stack.\n\nStill pinned in the reproducer, found with the new `ASH_GC_DEBUG_ROOTS=1` report (per root group KB kept and trace time; for any object of 1 MB or more, the chain of words from a root): a stale slot in main's frame holding the dropped Canvas, an integer on the stack that falls inside a buffer, and an Int field (a colour) of a heap object. The last kind is what scanning class instances by field layout would remove; the layouts exist (mark_bits per class). Not started: wait for ashui's chains to see which kind dominates in the demo.\n\nNo work yet on pauses beyond mark cost: still no minor or incremental collection on wasm (the barrier is page protection).","files":null}]}